    "created_at": "2016-04-15T15:50:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-15T15:50:37Z",
    "body": "Yes. For Bluetooth it's maybe more obvious to the website that it might not be talking to the device it expects, since it only gets to filter on service UUIDs and names, and has to let the user select the actual device, but USB also lets the user select the device.\n\nThis is probably worth adding to the Security Considerations sections of both specs, but doesn't seem like a big risk for either?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
