    "created_at": "2016-04-15T15:58:38Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-04-15T15:58:38Z",
    "body": "Host software (kernel drivers, user applications and now web apps) should always assume that the device it is talking to could be malicious. It's clear that a lot of host software has been written with the assumption that the device is trustworthy and the resulting security vulnerabilities are well documented. A USB (or Bluetooth) device needs to be treated the same as any other network endpoint and have its input verified and sanitized by the software receiving it.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
